CrystalCat said:
but how do we get from there to the icons showing up on the battler?
I know there's a show icon script call, but you choose the X and Y for that, rather than it showing on the actor.
if all else fails, i do have SRD's hudmaker, like i said before so i suppose i could make all of the icons for each character and only have them appear when "actorElemIcon" is set to something...?
Click to expand...
Set up the icons for each element in the plugin parameters
HUDMaker is probably the easiest lift to do this if you're already using that. You would only need to create an Icon HUD Component
For each actor in battle. Then in IconIndex -> Code
Use:
Spoiler:
HUDMaker > Icon Component > IconIndex > Code
const battler = $gameParty.members()[0];
if (battler){
const actorElement = PK_ElementImpact.getCurrentElement(battler);
const actorElemIcon = PK_ElementImpact.elementIcon(actorElement);
return actorElemIcon;
}
return 0;
Update the party index for each actor
`PK_ElementImpact.getCurrentElement` returns "0" by default if no element is found/no icon associated. So it should work without that if check, but HUDMaker is wonky sometimes when changing from Map to Battle so throwing in there just in case.

